#pragma code_page(65001)
// res/lang/ne.rc -- Nepali (नेपाली), the strings of the interface for `[general] language = "ne"`.
//
// Stage E108, group A: the translation is an adaptation (decision 198.14), not a literal one.
// The terms of Windows are those of Windows in Nepali; the honorific imperative of Nepali
// (-नुहोस्: गर्नुहोस्, छान्नुहोस्) addresses the reader without gender; the first person of
// Nepali has no gender, so the author's voice needs no masculine form (RULES 14). The sentence
// ends with the danda (।). Where each string is seen and how much room it has is
// res/lang/context.tsv.
//
// ⚠ In an .rc string a backslash is an escape -- one backslash is written as two -- and a double
// quote inside a string is written as two double quotes. The code page line above is this
// file's own: without it rc.exe reads the file in the ANSI code page, silently.

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Nepali — `[general] language = "ne"`.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
